---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import SkeletonDemo from "../../components/SkeletonDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Skeleton"
  description="Pulsing placeholders that hold the shape of content while it loads."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Skeleton</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Holds the space of content that is still loading. Use it for rows, titles,
    panels, and table cells, so the page does not jump when data arrives.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><SkeletonDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Skeleton usage"
      code={`import { Skeleton, SkeletonGroup } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/skeleton";

<SkeletonGroup label="Loading projects" gap="lg">
  <Skeleton />
  <Skeleton />
  <Skeleton />
</SkeletonGroup>

<SkeletonGroup label="Loading workflow diagram">
  <Skeleton shape="title" />
  <Skeleton shape="panel" />
</SkeletonGroup>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Skeleton</code> renders an empty <code>div</code>. <code>shape</code
      >
      sets its size:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>"line"</code>, the default: 16px tall, full width.</li>
      <li><code>"title"</code>: 24px tall, two thirds wide.</li>
      <li><code>"avatar"</code>: a 32px circle.</li>
      <li><code>"panel"</code>: 128px tall, full width.</li>
      <li><code>"checkbox"</code>: a 16px box.</li>
      <li>
        <code>"action"</code>: a 28px square, the size of a small icon button.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <code>className</code>, <code>style</code>, and <code>data-*</code>
      attributes pass through, so you can set a custom size or a width variable for
      one placeholder.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>SkeletonGroup</code> stacks skeletons in a <code>status</code>
      region. <code>gap</code> is <code>"sm"</code> (8px), <code>"md"</code>
      (12px, the default), or <code>"lg"</code> (16px). Use <code>render</code>
      to change the element, for example to a <code>section</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Table rows</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Placeholder table rows"
      code={`<Table aria-label="Records" data={rows} columns={columns} getRowId={(row) => row.id} loading={isLoading} />`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Visible status text</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Group with a sentence"
      code={`<SkeletonGroup gap="sm">
  <p>Loading GitHub accounts…</p>
  <Skeleton />
  <Skeleton />
</SkeletonGroup>`}
    />
    <p>
      When the wait needs words, put them inside the group and leave out
      <code>label</code>. The sentence then names the region.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Menu rows</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Icon and capped text bar"
      code={`<div className="flex h-8 items-center gap-2 px-2">
  <Skeleton className="size-4 rounded-md" />
  <Skeleton
    className="h-4 max-w-(--skeleton-width) flex-1"
    style={{ "--skeleton-width": "72%" } as CSSProperties}
  />
</div>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Each skeleton is <code>aria-hidden</code>, so screen readers skip it.
      <code>SkeletonGroup</code> has <code>role="status"</code>. Its
      <code>label</code> becomes the accessible name and is also rendered as visually
      hidden text, such as “Loading projects…”. Skeletons are not focusable and ignore
      the pointer.
    </p>
    <p>
      The pulse runs every 1.6 seconds and stops when reduced motion is
      requested. In forced colors mode each skeleton gets a visible border.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The fill is <code>--sprout-secondary</code>. Corners follow
      <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
